Nested Class in C++

 *Description* 

This C++ program demonstrates the concept of a nested class. The "Department" class is defined inside the "University" class and is used to store and display the department name.

 *Concepts Used* 

- Classes and Objects
- Nested Class
- Constructor
- Encapsulation
- "std::string"
- "std::move()"

 *Working* 

- "University" is the outer class.
- "Department" is a class defined inside "University".
- The "Department" class contains a private "name" variable.
- Its constructor initializes the department name.
- The "display()" function prints the department name.
- The nested class object is created using "University::Department".

 *Sample Output* 

Department: Artificial Intelligence and Data Science

 *Objective* 

To understand how a nested class can be declared inside another class and accessed using the scope resolution operator "::".
